      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $255^\\circ=300^\\circ-45^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y)=\\sin x\\cos y-\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(255^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(300^\\circ-45^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(300^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right)-\\cos\\left(300^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(45^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{-\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
